{"name":"Brickyard","hex":"#ab6a64","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brickyard","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place where bricks are, or once were, produced or distributed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brickyard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brickyard","blocks":[{"text":"A brickyard or brickfield is a place or yard where bricks are made, fired, and stored, or sometimes sold or otherwise distributed from. Brick makers work in a brick yard. A brick yard may be constructed near natural sources of clay or on or near a construction site if necessity or design requires the bricks to be made locally."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Fotothek_df_tg_0007580_Bauwesen_%5E_Baustoff_%5E_Ziegel.jpg/330px-Fotothek_df_tg_0007580_Bauwesen_%5E_Baustoff_%5E_Ziegel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brickyard"},{"title":"Brickyard (East Chicago)","blocks":[{"text":"The Brickyard was a neighborhood in the Indiana Harbor section of East Chicago, Indiana, near the intersection of Kennedy Avenue and Gannister Court. It stood for much of the 20th century, housing approximately 30 primarily African American families, until the City of East Chicago demolished it in the mid-1990s due to contamination from the adjacent Pollution Control Industries (PCI) hazardous waste mixing facility."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brickyard_(East_Chicago)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Kabul_brickyards.jpg/500px-Kabul_brickyards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Kabul_brickyards.jpg/1280px-Kabul_brickyards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Kabul_brickyards.jpg/500px-Kabul_brickyards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Domed kilns on ancient brickyards in Kabul","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKabul_brickyards.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Cegly03.jpg/500px-Cegly03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Cegly03.jpg/500px-Cegly03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A brickyard in postwar Poland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACegly03.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Anderson_%26_Ballards_Brick_yard%2C_circa_1877_-_DPLA_-_be751b5561432892543fd5a6c6c691a4.jpeg/500px-Anderson_%26_Ballards_Brick_yard%2C_circa_1877_-_DPLA_-_be751b5561432892543fd5a6c6c691a4.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Anderson_%26_Ballards_Brick_yard%2C_circa_1877_-_DPLA_-_be751b5561432892543fd5a6c6c691a4.jpeg/500px-Anderson_%26_Ballards_Brick_yard%2C_circa_1877_-_DPLA_-_be751b5561432892543fd5a6c6c691a4.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A brickyard in Macon, GA, c.1877","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnderson_%26_Ballards_Brick_yard%2C_circa_1877_-_DPLA_-_be751b5561432892543fd5a6c6c691a4.jpeg"}],"sounds":{}}}